    "id": "doc_1788288097537_kdz2c",
    "text": " solo flights, and inefficient commuting patterns.\n\n## Personal Vehicles & Maintenance\n- **Tire Pressure Optimization**: Maintaining proper tire inflation improves fuel efficiency by up to 3%. Under-inflated tires increase fuel consumption and wear out tires 15% faster.\n- **Aggressive Driving & Speeding**: Hard acceleration, rapid braking, and driving over 60 mph (100 km/h) reduce fuel economy by 15% to 30% on highways.\n- **Vehicle Weight Reduction**: Removing unnecessary cargo from the boot/trunk saves approximately 1% in fuel efficiency for every 45 kg (100 lbs) removed.",
